      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "answer": "Current law sets the state minimum wage at $17.00 per hour. The measure reduces it to $15.00 per hour beginning in 2028.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "answer": "Minimum-wage workers bear the cost through lower hourly earnings. Employers of minimum-wage labor benefit from reduced payroll costs.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "answer": "Employers may respond to lower labor costs by hiring more staff, increasing employee hours, or reducing price increases for consumers. Conversely, workers earning the minimum wage may seek higher-paying jobs or work more hours to maintain their income.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "answer": "The measure addresses the potential problem of high labor costs burdening employers, which can lead to reduced hiring or higher consumer prices. The mechanism lowers the wage floor to reduce these costs.",
      "disputed": false
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "§1",
      "question_id": "Q7",
      "answer": "The effect of minimum wage changes on hiring and investment is disputed. Some researchers find that lower minimum wages encourage businesses to create more jobs and hire more workers, while others find that changes in the minimum wage have minimal impact on employment levels but significantly affect workers' overall earnings.",
      "disputed": true
    }
